Offline build cache
===================

This directory contains pre-downloaded archives used for offline/airgapped
builds when the Go module proxy or a download host is unavailable.

Contents:
  go-sqlite3-v1.14.22.zip  — github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 v1.14.22
  draw.war                 — (optional, not in git) draw.io release archive

draw.io for the container build
-------------------------------

The image build downloads draw.war from the jgraph/drawio release. On networks
where that download is blocked or keeps dropping (curl exit 56), fetch it once
by any means and drop it here — the build uses the local copy instead:

  curl -fL -o vendor-cache/draw.war \
    https://github.com/jgraph/drawio/releases/download/v30.0.4/draw.war
  ./kanban.sh build

Or build without the diagram editor entirely:

  SKIP_DRAWIO=1 ./kanban.sh build

Usage (manual build without network):

  mkdir -p $(go env GOMODCACHE)/cache/download/github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3/@v
  cp vendor-cache/go-sqlite3-v1.14.22.zip \
     $(go env GOMODCACHE)/cache/download/github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3/@v/v1.14.22.zip
  GOFLAGS=-mod=mod GONOSUMCHECK=github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3 go build ./cmd/server

Or use GOPROXY=file:// to point Go at a local module mirror.
